PAD is about {tag 'tags'/}

<p>
A single {tag 'tag', single/} or 
an open/close combination {tag 'tag'/} .... {tag 'tag', close/}

<p>
A single tag is closed with a trailing <b>/</b> character. A tag written without it opens a pair,
and its closing tag has to follow: under the strict syntax check a tag that has neither is an
error - <code>the pair {open/}echo{close/} never closes - a single tag is written {open/}echo .../{close/}</code> -
and the lenient walk reads it as a single tag. The slash may stand in front of an opening pipe
as well: <code>{open/}echo $x /| upper{close/}</code>. The variable forms - <code>{open/}$x{close/}</code>,
<code>{open/}!x{close/}</code>, <code>{open/}#x{close/}</code> ... - are never pairs and take no slash.

<br><br>
